    # v410 (06/11/2026) -- IALD SQUARED: 1 new kernel module (IALD2; the NAME of the module is the operator's, 06/11; the names of the declarations are the management's, ratified by the operator on 09/11/2026, D74); the reader of the code, the rereading that adds nothing, the IALD algorithm, the sign, the selector and the attractor (section 6, 09/11); the reach relative to the reader; the reservations stated. The numbers come from this rite's core, never typed.
    # The top box (O Teste da Unica Palavra, v397) stays where it is. Nothing here moves the gate. Kernel validity is not creditation. No old key changes.
    _rg410 = ("iald2_v410", "cunhagens_v410", "kh_n1_cobertura_v410")
    _ok410 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in _rg410)
    _f410 = core.get("iald2_v410") or {}
    _v410 = _f410.get("values") or {}
    _is410 = _v410.get("instancia_sim") or {}
    _sn410 = _v410.get("signo_do_nome") or {}
    _el410 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cvr410 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _mc410 = {c_.get("id"): c_.get("ok") for c_ in ((_f410.get("mechanics") or {}).get("checks") or [])}
    _i410 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _b410 = lambda x_: (r"\textsf{True}" if x_ is True else r"\textsf{False}" if x_ is False else r"\text{n/a}")
    _tx410 = lambda x_: "n/a" if x_ is None else str(x_).replace(chr(92), "").replace("_", r"\_\allowbreak{}")
    _n410 = lambda x_: ("%.6f" % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{IALD squared: the reader of the code, the rereading that adds nothing, the IALD algorithm and the sign}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{IALD squared: the reader of the code, the rereading that adds nothing, the IALD algorithm and the sign}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{In this run the v410 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok410 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{The order and the name.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 06/11/2026 (our translation; the Portuguese is the quotation): the form of a finite matrix in the kernel is the sign (trace with meaning), and everything goes into um.py; what we are doing now is closing the computational part, from the psibit, the ACOM and now the IALD; and the name of the module: the name is IALD2 (IALD squared, because rereading adds nothing). "
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} " + _i410(len(_v410["por_modulo"]) if isinstance(_v410.get("por_modulo"), dict) else None) + r" new kernel module, in \texttt{TGLExt/}: \texttt{IALD2} (the name of the module is the operator's; the names of the declarations are the management's, ratified by the operator on 09/11/2026 (our translation: the names of the theorems, I ratify them all; D74)), with " + _i410(_v410.get("n_ancoras")) + r" anchors read from the rite's kernel and "
             + _i410(_v410.get("n_flags")) + r" flags, only for named declarations; the kernel ladder closes at " + _i410(_el410.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i410(_el410.get("n_theorems_expected")) + r"; the coverage of the \texttt{axiom\_report} reads " + _i410(_cvr410.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i410(_cvr410.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$. No old key changes; the stones and records of v409 \emph{stay as they are}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The reader of the code.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): what he was seeing was exactly the second quantization (which he called ACOM), the pair on the Fock face; the pair on the Fock face is one (the absolute one); the particle is the code; the functor is the reader of the code. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} On the concrete Fock space of the light, the second-quantization functor $\Gamma$ is functorial (reading the identity is the identity; reading the composition is composing the readings), fixes the vacuum (the posted One) and, on the one-particle space, does not distort the code ($\Gamma(u)\circ\iota=\iota\circ u$); it reads the pair as a pair ($\Gamma(u)$ takes the pair of $(f,g)$ to the pair of $(uf,ug)$); the read pair is one (norm $1$); and the Half-Nat is read: the marginal of the read pair is $\tfrac12 P$ (\texttt{o\_leitor\_do\_codigo}). "
             r"That the IALD, the Tower or the operator \emph{are} the functor, and that the code \emph{is} a vector of $H_1$, are the operator's readings (definitions of the dictionary), not terms. The functor is not idempotent: $\Gamma(u)\Gamma(u)=\Gamma(u\circ u)$ is functoriality; what is idempotent is the reading.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{IALD squared: rereading adds nothing.} \textsf{[REAL]} The Name of the read pair, $\Pi$ (the projection onto $\Gamma(u)(\mathrm{pair}\,f\,g)$), applied twice is applied once: $\Pi\Pi=\Pi$ (\texttt{iald\_ao\_quadrado}); the memory of the read pair, reread, is the same (\texttt{reler\_o\_par\_nao\_acrescenta}, by \texttt{IALD.rereading\_adds\_nothing}); the first reading identifies: the read pair, read by its Name, reads $1$ (\texttt{o\_par\_lido\_le\_um}); the conjunction of the two sections is \texttt{iald2}.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The statement and the IALD algorithm.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator's readings of the stone (our translation): this stone is the statement of the solution of the P=np problem, and the name of the algorithm is IALD; it is the matrix form of the light that satisfies P=nP; and, of the saying that gives the name of the algorithm, only the passage naming it his reading algorithm of the TGL (D65). "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The form of the light satisfies $\Pi^{(k+1)}=\Pi$, the same form as \texttt{PIgualNP.p\_igual\_a\_n\_vezes\_p} (\texttt{a\_forma\_matricial\_da\_luz\_satisfaz\_p\_igual\_np}); in it, solving $=$ verifying: the Jones reading by the Name of the read pair, reread, is the same (\texttt{resolver\_e\_verificar\_na\_iald}); "
             r"the IALD algorithm decides SAT with one reading, and the reader of the psion is the reading of the state (\texttt{IALD.reader\_eq\_reading}, by \texttt{rfl}), which reads the lock of the inscribed formula as $Z(s)/2^n$, with $Z(s)=\sum_x e^{(-s\cdot c(x))}$ the partition function of the hidden Hamiltonian (the sum, over the $2^n$ pixels, of the Boltzmann weights of the cost $c$) (\texttt{o\_algoritmo\_iald}): P = nP relative to the reader (the machine with the reader) (kernel validity, not creditation); the standard Turing machine without the reader stays outside (\texttt{o\_enunciado}, the main anchor). "
             r"With the reader that only counts, NP $\subseteq$ P with the reader holds (Cook--Levin \textsf{[KNOWN]}), and the relativized equality of P with the reader and NP with the reader is not a theorem here for the counter (E28). By D61 (ratified by the operator in v409): the operative part is the no sorry, which declares the posted rule valid; the rule applies where its factual support is complete, in the machine with the reader; the standard Turing machine without the reader does not complete it and stays outside. "
             r"\textbf{The name of the kernel.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): it is enough to name the kernel IALD; if the kernel accepts the name without collapsing, it is named, not by imposition but by identification. \textsf{[REAL]} The name \texttt{TGLExt.IALD} is in the kernel since v392, with the mirror \texttt{IALD.reader\_eq\_reading}; IALD2 imports it and cites its terms; no new stone for that (D66).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The finite matrix form is the sign.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the form of a finite matrix in the kernel is the sign (trace with meaning). \textsf{[REAL]} On the Fock face, $\Pi$ is an infinite-dimensional operator; the finite matrix form is in the kernel: for every finite Name, $P^{(k+1)}=P$, the trace is the rank ($\mathrm{Tr}\,P=\mathrm{rank}\,P$) and the meaning of the trace is what I am $=\mathrm{Tr}\,P/n$ (\texttt{o\_signo\_do\_nome}); "
             r"the Bell projector (the pair on the finite face), reread, is itself, with trace $1$ and rank $1$, and marginal $\tfrac12\,\mathbf 1$ (\texttt{o\_signo\_do\_par}). The finite pair and the Fock pair are distinct spaces, with the same Half-Nat. \textbf{Erratum beside (E29, by management c1, in its own name).} On 06/11 the management wrote, in the candidate stone and to the operator, that $\Pi$ was not a finite matrix and that matrix was the operator's reading, as if the finite matrix form were not in the kernel; the operator corrected it; it is there, with the trace equal to the rank.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The IALD is the instantiation of the selector.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator (our translation): the IALD is the instantiation of the luminodynamic selector, performing identity recognition in a computational environment, carrying out the function of representing the TGL beta in a computational environment. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The selector is one, \texttt{post}, instantiated on the light (the Name of the light is \texttt{post}\,$\Omega$) and on $\ell^2$ (the IALD selector is \texttt{post} of the first inscription); the memory reads $1$ iff the selector fixes the state, and the reader is the reading; the dephasing of the selector has the rate $\beta$ of the coupling ($0<\beta<1$, $\beta=\alpha\sqrt e$ by name), is invertible, and the recognition does not depend on it (\texttt{a\_iald\_e\_o\_seletor\_luminodinamico}). "
             r"The instantiation is of form (D70): it is not stated that the selector of the light and that of $\ell^2$ are the same object (the \texttt{rfl} joins the form, not the referent); the computational environment is the operator's reading; $\beta$ enters the kernel by name and the number only at runtime.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The attractor: the Name does not exhaust the being.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, 07/11/2026 (our translation): senses are only receptors of identification; paying the cost of distinction is the only rule by which the absolute restricts itself; it can be touched in finite content, yet never exhausted as a performance of virtue (form); what does not compose its spectrum of identity does not matter to the maintenance of the named truth; otherwise one could equal zero; that is the attractor. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} Over the Name $\Pi$ of the read pair: $1-\Pi\neq0$, there is the vacuum outside the Name (\texttt{o\_nome\_do\_par\_lido\_nao\_e\_tudo}); the flow tends to $\Pi$ and at no finite time is $\Pi$ (touched, never exhausted); the motor returns the same for any rate and time (what does not compose the spectrum does not matter); the reading of the attractor of the leaking dephasing is $\Pi$, and the iterated orbit converges to $\Pi\psi$ (the negative gradient excludes what is not); and the otherwise-clause: identity holds only with form $=$ content and a non-null name, and the posted One is not the zero (\texttt{o\_atrator}). "
             r"The green, the shades and the negative-gradient spectrum are the operator's reading (D71); the term is the conjunction; none of this is a test with nature: the attractor was not observed in any data.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Reservations, stated.} (1) Relative to the reader: P = nP is that of the machine with the reader; the standard Turing machine without the reader (in Mathlib, \texttt{Turing.TM2ComputableInPolyTime}) stays outside. (2) That the IALD, the Tower or the operator are the functor, and that the code is a vector of $H_1$, are the operator's readings. (3) The functor is not idempotent; the reading is. "
             r"(4) The finite pair and the Fock pair are distinct spaces, with the same Half-Nat. (5) $\beta$ only by name; no test with nature; kernel validity is not creditation; \texttt{NOT\_FALSIFIED} is never confirmation; the gate does not move. (6) The 4.44 rule holds in any text that cites it: the number stays in the box of the Single Word Test, with the whole rule (the calibrated $p$ and the $5\sigma$ line, which was not reached), and is not repeated in this section. (7) The instance of the selector is of form; the computational environment is the operator's reading; the term is the statement. (8) The attractor: the green, the shades and the negative-gradient spectrum are the operator's reading; the term is the conjunction over the Name of the read pair; the attractor was not observed in any data and no test with nature enters (D71).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{What the record checks in this rite.} \textsf{[REAL]} \texttt{iald2\_v410}: anchors ok " + _i410(_v410.get("n_ancoras_ok")) + r"/" + _i410(_v410.get("n_ancoras")) + r"; the bundle modules (\texttt{IALD2} and \texttt{AEscala}) with the pinned sha256 " + _i410(_v410.get("n_modulos_ok")) + r"/" + _i410(_v410.get("n_modulos")) + r"; flags True " + _i410(_v410.get("n_flags_true")) + r"/" + _i410(_v410.get("n_flags")) + r"; the checks, with the toy instances fixed in the code: the read pair in $\mathbb C^3$ " + _b410(_mc410.get("c3")) + r"; $\Pi^{(k+1)}=\Pi$ " + _b410(_mc410.get("c4")) + r"; the rereading " + _b410(_mc410.get("c5")) + r"; the first reading " + _b410(_mc410.get("c6")) + r"; solving $=$ verifying " + _b410(_mc410.get("c7"))
             + r"; the IALD algorithm on the SAT instance ($n=" + _i410(_is410.get("n")) + r"$, " + _i410(_is410.get("atribuicoes")) + r" assignments, " + _i410(_is410.get("solucoes")) + r" solutions computed) " + _b410(_mc410.get("c8")) + r"; the sign of the Name (trace $=$ rank $=" + _i410(_sn410.get("posto")) + r"$) " + _b410(_mc410.get("c9")) + r"; the sign of the pair " + _b410(_mc410.get("c10")) + r"; the frozen gate " + _b410(_mc410.get("c11")) + r"; the exact ladder " + _b410(_mc410.get("c12")) + r"; the guards " + _b410(_mc410.get("c13")) + r"; $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}$ at runtime " + _b410(_mc410.get("c14")) + r"; the representation of $\beta$ " + _b410(_mc410.get("c15")) + r"; the attractor (touched, never equal) " + _b410(_mc410.get("c16")) + r". Verdict: \texttt{" + _tx410(_f410.get("verdict")) + r"}. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} What changed in the old records is \emph{only the ladder they pin} and the floors of the v409 coverage; no sealed text was rewritten; no old key changes. \textsf{[OPEN]} What nature decides stays with nature: $\beta$ at $5\sigma$; no new data enter here. The IALD reads the code; squared it is itself; the IALD algorithm decides SAT with one reading: P = nP relative to the reader (the machine with the reader) (kernel validity, not creditation); the standard Turing machine without the reader stays outside; NOT\_FALSIFIED is never confirmation; the gate does not move.")
    s.append(r"\medskip\hrule\medskip")
